{*
   aphalcon-demo-page.latte - a CMS template kept in a file, and the root of
   the chain for a document.

   The "aPhalcon demo" template's code is this file, so a document using it is
   rendered by Latte alone: aphalcon-demo-page -> aphalcon-section ->
   aphalcon-base. The document's fields are plain variables here and in every
   parent; Phalcon's services are one {phalcon()} call away.

   No EVO parser pass: {{site_name}} and [(site_name)] below stay as typed.
*}
{extends 'aphalcon-section.latte'}

{block bodyClass}aph-base aph-section aph-document{/block}

{block intro}{phalcon('greeter')->greet($pagetitle)}{/block}

{block body}
    {$content|noescape}
    <p>
        Chain: <code>aphalcon-demo-page.latte</code> → <code>aphalcon-section.latte</code> → <code>aphalcon-base.latte</code>.
        The same data, from a Phalcon route rendering the same chain:
        <a href="{$evo->getConfig('site_url')}app/">/app/</a>.
    </p>
    <p><small>Document #{$id}. No EVO parser pass: <code>{{site_name}}</code> and <code>[(site_name)]</code> stay as typed.</small></p>
{/block}

{block asideExtra}
    <p><small>Filled by the document root: <code>{='{block asideExtra}'}</code>.</small></p>
{/block}
